Trigger efficiency is defined as the fraction of non-photonic electron that have an associated BEMC tower adc value above the trigger threshold. In the analysis, we used data from different high tower triggers which use energy deposition in BEMC towers as trigger threshold. To estimate their trigger efficiency, use the minimum-bias trigger as reference, which counts the total number of events. Then normalize the trigger events properly according to their prescale factor and luminosity.

